error[NK1102]: This lambda can fail, but `fn()` says the code it names never fails.
   --> tests/a_failing_lambda_where_the_type_does_not_fail_is_refused.nika:22:5
    |
 22 |     let g: fn() = fn { throw Bad::Oops }
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: A function type without `throws` cannot fail, so a lambda that can is not of that type.
    = help: Write `fn() throws` as the type, or handle the failure inside the lambda with `… catch { … }`.
